  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want the legacy Catégories list (flat, with icons and \"N sous-forums\", sub-forum picker in the topic list) and the persisted segmented filter Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus, so that I find my lists where I know them.\n\n### Scope\n\nShipped today: collapsible sections without icons, and no filter. Option A for both (operator \"preserve what works\"). Milestone: **M2**; promote it to M1 only if the TestFlight testers must find their list there (the orchestrator decides).\n\n- Milestone: **M2** (operator decisions of 2026-11-02 on [#379](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379): UXD-05, UXD-06). Follow-up of LOT-082 (#100). GAP 020, 021, 022, 023 in `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`.\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · a small (a) item (a port of the legacy behaviour), not an evolution.\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master` @ 2440d79): the GAP rows above cite the files and symbols. Tracked by [#413](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/413).\n\n### Depends on\n\n- the merged lots above (done)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The behaviour matches the legacy app at 2440d79 (cited in the PR), and nothing else changes.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, App/README.md and the spec of the lots above. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Refs`/`Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; the app code starts with the `// Port of … @ 2440d79` comment (AGENTS.md §4).\n\n### Device comparison (operator, 2026-11-10, iPhone, dark mode)\n\nThe operator compared the legacy app and SwiftHFR side by side on the Catégories tab; the target is the legacy screen.\n\n| Element | Legacy (target) | SwiftHFR (`dev-swift`, today) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Container | Inset grouped list: one rounded card, lighter background than the page | Plain list straight on the black page, no card |\n| Category icon | One white glyph per category, on the left (chip, keyboard, laptop, wrench, circuit, phone/tablet, Apple logo, camera, game pad, Windows, Wi-Fi…) | None |\n| Subtitle | \"N sous-forums\" in secondary grey under the name | None |\n| Name | Primary white, regular | Secondary grey |\n| Separators | Thin separators between rows, inset after the icon | None |\n| Chevron | Discreet grey | Bright white |\n| Title | \"Categories\" | \"Catégories\" (keep the accented one: French UI strings) |\n| Top bar | Account avatar on the left, refresh button on the right | Account avatar on the right only, no refresh |\n\nAcceptance additions:\n- [ ] The Catégories screen matches the legacy column above: inset grouped card, icon, name, \"N sous-forums\", inset separators, grey chevron (light and dark, Dynamic Type XL).\n- [ ] The icon set and the \"N sous-forums\" count come from the legacy sources (file:line @ `87fe0d1c`), not guessed; any icon not in legacy is named in the PR.\n- [ ] Top bar: the avatar and refresh placement follow legacy, or the PR states why it differs (UXD).\n\nIn progress: PR #744 (`chore/427-categories-legacy-list`), Mac session. Screenshots are on the operator's device (not attached: cloud upload not available).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
