   "updated_at": "2026-11-10T20:35:06Z",
   "body": "Operator device check, 2026-11-10 (SwiftHFR, Favoris tab, titled \"Drapeaux\"): **a category title in Favoris is not tappable.** Each section header shows the category name in secondary grey, a count and a collapse chevron, and nothing opens the category. Item 3 of #593 moved here, so this issue owns it.\n\nLegacy @ `87fe0d1c`, `HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift:343-370` (`headerTitleView`):\n- The header title is a `Button` or a `NavigationLink`, labelled \"Ouvrir le forum\" for VoiceOver, with the title in `.primary`.\n- It pushes `ForumTopicsListView(forum:, initialFlagOverride: .favorites, …)` (`:356-363`). The category opens with **Favoris** selected (`MainWindow.swift:395-396`: `initialFlagOverride ?? persistedGlobalFlag`). It does not overwrite the persisted filter.\n\nAcceptance addition:\n- [ ] In Favoris, tapping a category's title opens that category's topic list with the filter on Favoris, without changing the persisted global filter. The collapse chevron keeps collapsing. VoiceOver reads \"Ouvrir le forum\". The title is in primary colour, as legacy.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
